---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="workgraph — task graphs for humans and agents"
  description="Work fast. Task graphs for humans and agents. Self-organizing, git-friendly, no server, no account."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-16 pb-16">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <header class="mb-16">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-zinc-50 leading-tight mb-4 font-mono">
        workgraph
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-text-secondary font-mono leading-relaxed">
        work fast<br />
        task graphs for humans and agents<br />
        self-organizing process flowgraphs<br />
        <span class="text-text-tertiary">cybernetic autopoietic stigmergic medium</span>
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Positioning Statement -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <p class="text-lg text-text-primary leading-relaxed">
        Building enormous things requires organizing at the same scale.
        Workgraph is a dependency graph of tasks — completing one unblocks the next.
        A coordinator dispatches AI agents to ready work. Each agent receives context
        from upstream, executes autonomously, and reports results back to the graph.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mt-4">
        For teams and individuals who coordinate humans and AI agents on complex projects.
        No server, no account — just a <code class="bg-bg-tertiary px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm font-mono text-zinc-50">.workgraph/</code> directory in your repo.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Screencast -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <div class="screencast-container">
        <video
          autoplay
          loop
          muted
          playsinline
          class="screencast-video"
          poster="/demo.gif"
        >
          <source src="/demo.webm" type="video/webm" />
          <!-- Fallback for browsers without webm support -->
          <img src="/demo.gif" alt="Workgraph TUI demo" class="screencast-video" />
        </video>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Features -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-2 font-mono lowercase">dependency graphs</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
            Define tasks and their dependencies. Completing one unblocks the next.
            Supports cycles for iterative workflows.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-2 font-mono lowercase">agent isolation</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
            Each agent gets its own git worktree. Parallel execution without merge conflicts.
            Commit, push, and report back independently.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-2 font-mono lowercase">TUI dashboard</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
            Monitor the entire graph in real time. Inspect tasks, view agent logs,
            navigate dependencies — all from the terminal.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-2 font-mono lowercase">evaluation &amp; evolution</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">
            Agents are scored after each task. An evolver mutates and recombines
            the best performers. The organization improves itself.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Viz: Task Graph -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <pre class="viz-block"><span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg viz design-api

<span class="c-done">design-api  (done)</span>
├→ <span class="c-done">auth-module  (done)</span>
│ └→ <span class="c-open">integration  (open)</span> <span class="c-dim">←───────┐</span>
│   └→ <span class="c-open">deploy  (open)</span>            <span class="c-dim">│</span>
├→ <span class="c-ip">data-layer  (in-progress)</span> <span class="c-dim">────┤</span>
└→ <span class="c-ip">search-index  (in-progress)</span> <span class="c-dim">──┘</span></pre>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mt-4">
        <code class="bg-bg-tertiary px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm font-mono text-zinc-50">.workgraph/graph.jsonl</code> — git-friendly, no server, no account.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Cycles -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-4 font-mono lowercase">cycles</h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        Processes that repeat — CI, monitoring, convergence —
        are cycles in the graph. Each has a bound. Agents pick up
        where previous iterations left off.
      </p>
      <pre class="viz-block"><span class="c-open">run-tests  (open)</span> <span class="c-dim">↺ (iter 0/5) ←─┐</span>
└→ <span class="c-open">fix-failures  (open)</span>          <span class="c-dim">│</span>
  └→ <span class="c-open">push-check  (open)</span> <span class="c-dim">─────────┘</span></pre>
    </section>

    <!-- Organizational Synthesis -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-4 font-mono lowercase">organizational synthesis</h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        Agents have roles (what they do) and motivations (constraints
        on how). After each task, agents are evaluated. An evolver
        mutates and recombines the best performers. The organization
        restructures itself based on what works.
      </p>
      <pre class="viz-block"><span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg agency stats

  Role        Motivation   Avg  Count  Rating
  -------------------------------------------
  Programmer  Thorough    0.93     63    <span class="c-done">HIGH</span>
  Writer      Balanced    0.88     19    <span class="c-done">HIGH</span>
  Analyst     Balanced    0.88     22    <span class="c-done">HIGH</span></pre>
    </section>

    <!-- Graph Structure -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-4 font-mono lowercase">graph structure</h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        Fan-out decomposes work. Fan-in synchronizes it.
        Arcs on the right show convergence.
      </p>
      <pre class="viz-block"><span class="c-open">hub  (open)</span>
├→ <span class="c-open">spoke-1  (open)</span>
│ └→ <span class="c-open">collector  (open)</span> <span class="c-dim">←─┐</span>
├→ <span class="c-open">spoke-2  (open)</span> <span class="c-dim">──────┤</span>
├→ <span class="c-open">spoke-3  (open)</span> <span class="c-dim">──────┤</span>
└→ <span class="c-open">spoke-4  (open)</span> <span class="c-dim">──────┘</span></pre>
    </section>

    <!-- Install -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-zinc-50 mb-4 font-mono lowercase">get started</h2>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
        Install with <a href="https://rustup.rs" class="text-accent-primary hover:text-accent-hover underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors">Rust</a> (Linux, macOS, Windows):
      </p>
      <pre class="install-cmd">cargo install --git https://github.com/graphwork/workgraph</pre>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mt-6 mb-4">Then start a project:</p>
      <pre class="viz-block"><span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg init
<span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg add "Design the API"
<span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg add "Build backend" --after design-the-api
<span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg add "Write tests" --after build-backend
<span class="text-text-tertiary">$</span> wg service start --max-agents 3</pre>
      <p class="text-text-secondary mt-4">
        The service dispatches agents to ready tasks, evaluates
        results, evolves the agent population, and loops.
        You define structure. It does the rest.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Viz blocks - terminal aesthetic */
  .viz-block {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-variant-ligatures: none;
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-primary);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Install command - prominent */
  .install-cmd {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent-primary);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.875rem 1.25rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  /* Screencast */
  .screencast-container {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-primary);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
  }

  .screencast-video {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Feature cards */
  .feature-card {
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-primary);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* Status colors matching the original */
  .c-done { color: #22c55e; }
  .c-ip { color: #eab308; }
  .c-fail { color: #ef4444; }
  .c-open { color: #e5e7eb; }
  .c-dim { color: #6b7280; }
</style>
